{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FMapC3ParityExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FMapC3ParityExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.VhopfS_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.VhopfS_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapC3ParityExclusion.lean#L98-L99","doc":"The Hopf polynomial's value at the classical point `s = 1` is `−2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.VhopfS_not_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.VhopfS_not_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapC3ParityExclusion.lean#L92-L96","doc":"**The Hopf polynomial is NOT bar-even.** It differs from its bar image at\nthe witness point `s = 2` (`−34 ≠ −17/32`), so no bar-even object can equal\nit as a q-identity — only its `s = 1` *value* coincides. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.VhopfS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.VhopfS","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapC3ParityExclusion.lean#L89-L90","doc":"The skein-derived Hopf-link Jones polynomial in `s = √q`: `V(Hopf)(s) = −(s+s⁵)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.targetValue_generic_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.targetValue_generic_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapC3ParityExclusion.lean#L77-L87","doc":"**Genericity (scope-(a)).** Four unrelated bar-even D-quantities all equal\n`−2` at `q = 1` — `−[2]_q`, `−(q²+q⁻²)`, `−y₃ᴰ/y₂₁ᴰ = −(q⁴+1)/q²`, and\n`−1/(2y₂₁ᴰ)`. Matching the q=1 value distinguishes none of them, so it cannot\nforce the Hopf identification: the anti-fit genericity that refutes the\nbar-even-weight route. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.barOdd_traceD_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.barOdd_traceD_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapC3ParityExclusion.lean#L70-L73","doc":"**Route A, formalised.** The bar-odd part of the D two-row trace of any\ncrossing power `σ^k` vanishes at `q = 1` — an instance of `barOdd_at_one`, so\nit can never equal the bar-even `c₃ = −2` there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.traceD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.traceD","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapC3ParityExclusion.lean#L63-L68","doc":"The dimension-weighted convention-D two-row (Temperley–Lieb) Markov trace of\nthe crossing power `σ^k`: block `(3)` scalar `q^k`, block `(2,1)` eigenvalues\n`q^k, (−q⁻¹)^k`, weights `y₃ᴰ, y₂₁ᴰ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hopfValue_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hopfValue_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapC3ParityExclusion.lean#L57-L59","doc":"The Hopf value at the classical point is `−2` (bar-even, nonzero). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.hopfValue_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.hopfValue_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapC3ParityExclusion.lean#L50-L55","doc":"**The Hopf-link Jones value `−(q²+q⁻²)` is bar-EVEN**, so it is *not* an\nobstruction to the parity argument: it sits in the complementary channel to\nevery bar-odd construction. (`bar` sends `q ↦ q⁻¹`; `q²+q⁻²` is fixed.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.barOdd_ne_hopf_value_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.barOdd_ne_hopf_value_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapC3ParityExclusion.lean#L41-L48","doc":"**Parity exclusion of the bar-odd routes to `c₃`.** The bar-odd content of\nany construction is `0` at `q = 1`, but the c₃ target — the Hopf-link Jones\nvalue at `q = 1` — is `−2 ≠ 0`. So `c₃ = J_Hopf(1) = −2` cannot be the\nbar-odd content of any object: it is a **bar-EVEN q=1 shadow**. This is the\nsingle invariant behind the refutation of both route A (crossing term) and\nroute B (Z3 carrier); both are bar-odd, hence vanish here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.barOdd_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.barOdd_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapC3ParityExclusion.lean#L36-L39","doc":"**Any bar-odd part vanishes at the bar fixed point `q = 1`.** Since\n`(1 : ℝ)⁻¹ = 1`, `barOdd f 1 = (f 1 − f 1)/2 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.barOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.barOdd","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FMapC3ParityExclusion.lean#L32-L34","doc":"The bar-odd part of a function of `q` under the bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹`:\n`barOdd f q = (f q − f q⁻¹)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}